wgpu-hal: admit Borealis (VK_DRIVER_ID_AURORA_BOREALIS) for WebGPU

wgpu-hal hides every Vulkan driver reporting conformanceVersion.major == 0
unless it is MoltenVK or InstanceFlags::ALLOW_UNDERLYING_NONCOMPLIANT_ADAPTER
is set. Borealis (Aurora Silicon's Apple Silicon Vulkan driver, registered
Khronos driver ID 35) reports conformanceVersion 0.0.0.0 until a formal
Khronos submission is completed, causing Firefox WebGPU to either return
no adapter or silently fall back to CPU llvmpipe.

Admit driver ID 35 (VK_DRIVER_ID_AURORA_BOREALIS) alongside MoltenVK so
Firefox selects the hardware Borealis adapter by default on Apple Silicon.

--- a/third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/vulkan/adapter.rs	2026-11-25 01:28:57.893990292 +1100
+++ b/third_party/rust/wgpu-hal/src/vulkan/adapter.rs	2026-11-25 01:28:57.940885087 +1100
@@ -2374,6 +2374,8 @@
             if driver.conformance_version.major == 0 {
                 if driver.driver_id == vk::DriverId::MOLTENVK {
                     log::debug!("Adapter is not Vulkan compliant, but is MoltenVK, continuing");
+                } else if driver.driver_id == vk::DriverId::from_raw(35) {
+                    log::debug!("Adapter is not Vulkan compliant, but is Borealis, continuing");
                 } else if self
                     .shared
                     .flags
